# The public node's live policy rows (lane public-node, 2026-09-26): one
# `fn operator CONFIG policy set SLOT VALUE` per non-comment line, applied
# by deploy-fresh after `init` and before the first `run` (each row is a
# durable configuration record; a later `policy set` replaces it live).
# PRF-161's limits by name (books/public-exposure.lisp); specs/nntp.md
# "Public exposure" is the table. Absent rows take the public defaults on a
# listener off loopback; every row is written anyway, so `health` and the
# node record name the limits in force rather than a default.
#
# exposure-connections: the total a run admits is never above the run's
# max_connections, which is the constant 32 (books/native-config.lisp
# *fn-ncfg-default-max-connections*), one socket held back for the
# operator: 31 is the real ceiling, whatever docs/operator.md's example of
# 200 says (gap packet a).
exposure-connections 31
# 4, not the default 8: with 31 sockets, 8 per address lets four hosts fill
# the node; 4 lets a reader run a few connections and needs eight hosts.
exposure-per-address 4
exposure-steps-per-second 64
exposure-first-seconds 60
exposure-idle-seconds 600
exposure-auth-failures 10
exposure-posts-per-minute 60
# PKT-405: no read-only anonymous level exists; `open` would let an
# anonymous client POST. Every reader logs in.
anonymous none
# NNT-013: a login bound to a signing principal posts only as it; unbound
# logins (a newsreader) post as before.
posting-policy bound-logins
path-identity fn.fg-goose.online
